{
  "_": [
    "docs/design/FLOOR.md § 4.6 — THE ONE STATEMENT of how a layout and the installs the fleet",
    "reports compose into floors. Two runtimes implement it — App\\Building\\Building::compose()",
    "for the admin console and public/js/lobby/lobby-model.js floors() for the lobby — and both",
    "are held to every case here (Tests\\Feature\\Building, Tests\\Feature\\Lobby). A case is the",
    "RAW authored document (a list of floor records, each carrying its `rooms` — a mapping of",
    "install id to that room's RECORD, `{\"form\": …}` and, on a planned floor, `{\"origin\": …}`",
    "(card#9292) — and optionally its `label` (card#9273) and its `hallway`), the installs the",
    "fleet reports, and the floors that must come out: floor keys ascending, each floor's `label`",
    "(null where the layout names no label, and null on every implicit floor), rooms by install",
    "ascending, each room's `origin` where the floor is planned, and `reported` per room.",
    "⚠ A floor's `hallway` is deliberately NOT among them: it is a whole Tiled document that only",
    "the floor SCREEN draws, and the cases pin both runtimes to leaving it in the layout.",
    "Add a case here and both suites gain it; a rule that lives in one runtime and not the other",
    "is what this file exists to red."
  ],
